    "reply": "The records retrieved for rs334 include a variant record whose clinical significance is listed as not-provided, protective, likely-benign, pathogenic, other [1]. The literature variant name linked to this search is c.20A>T [2]. None of the findings names a specific condition, so the associated disease cannot be stated from these records [1].\n\n## Variant identity\n\nThe retrieved literature name for the variant is c.20A>T [2]. This is a single-nucleotide substitution notation, but the findings do not give the gene or transcript it is written against [2].\n\n## Clinical significance\n\nThe variant record carries mixed clinical significance assertions: not-provided, protective, likely-benign, pathogenic, other [1]. The combination of pathogenic and protective calls suggests different submitters or contexts, but the findings do not say which condition each assertion refers to [1].\n\n## Other matched variants\n\nThe search also returned other variants with similar identifiers. One is rs334348 [3]. Another is rs334353 [4]. A third is rs334773 [6]. The search also returned c.-50T>C [5]. These appear to be separate variants that matched the rs334 prefix, so they should not be read as evidence about rs334 itself [3].",
